# Frontend test mocking (Vitest)

**Disclosure:** Tier C (glob — any `frontend/**` edit). Parent: `.cursor/rules/test-doubles.mdc`. Hotline: `.cursor/rules/harness-hotline.mdc`. Strategy: `docs/testing_strategy.md`.

## Layout

- Specs live under **`frontend/tests/`** (`vite.config.ts` `include: ["tests/**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}"]`).
- Import product code with a relative path into `src/`, e.g. `import { App } from "../src/main"`.

## Default

- Render **real components** under test; mock only at **trust boundaries** (network, browser APIs).
- Assert **RTL state**: `toHaveTextContent`, `toHaveValue`, `toBeChecked`, `toBeVisible` — not `vi.fn()` call counts alone.

## Network — stub `fetch`, not the component

This SPA talks to the API via `fetch` (no separate `api/client` module). Prefer a **router-style** `vi.stubGlobal("fetch", …)` that returns canned JSON by URL (see `frontend/tests/App.test.tsx` `mockFetchRouter`, `frontend/tests/ServicesPage.test.tsx`).

```typescript
// Reject — assert call wiring only
expect(fetchMock).toHaveBeenCalledWith("/api/<resources>")

// Prefer — stub fetch; assert what the user sees
vi.stubGlobal("fetch", vi.fn(async (input: RequestInfo | URL) => {
  const url = String(input)
  if (url.includes("/<resources>")) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify([{ id: "one", name: "HQ", status: "active" }]), {
      status: 200,
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    })
  }
  return new Response("not found", { status: 404 })
}))
// …render… then:
expect(await screen.findByText("HQ")).toBeInTheDocument()
```

When GET and write must stay consistent in one test, keep **one in-memory object** both stub branches read/write (stateful fake), then assert DOM after the write.

## What belongs in Vitest vs E2E

| Scenario | Vitest | E2E (`e2e_test/`) |
|---|---|---|
| Pure helpers (`<resource>Stats`, `jsonLeafPatch`, `batchLatencyStats`) | Real module test under `frontend/tests/` | — |
| Component DOM (JsonTree, Services cards, API try-it UI) | Real render + fetch stub | — |
| Create / Load / Archive / nested add / History across Compose | Thin coverage OK | Required when `docs/testing_strategy.md` E2E triggers apply |

## Async defaults

- Do not rely on `useEffect` + `findBy*` alone to paper over empty initial render — fix sync derivation or `waitFor` on **user-visible value** (`toHaveTextContent` / `toHaveValue`), not on mock calls.

## Test file comments

When a Vitest file still stubs network, add a one-line header pointing to the E2E that owns full-stack proof, e.g.:

`Full stack: e2e_test/<resources>/test_<feature>_tab.py`

## Reject in frontend tests

- Asserting `toHaveBeenCalledWith` without a DOM/output assertion for user-facing behaviour.
- Duplicating an E2E-only flow entirely in Vitest with every route mocked.
- Mocking the component under test or its direct util instead of testing it for real.
- Putting new specs under `frontend/src/**` — use `frontend/tests/`.
